<title>FRANCE: Bouygues unit wins 750 mln Ffr contract.</title>
<headline>Bouygues unit wins 750 mln Ffr contract.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>French construction company Bouygues said on Tuesday its unit, Dragages et Travaux Publics (DTP), had won a 750 million franc contract to build maintenance and hangar workshops for the planned new Chek Lap Kok airport in Hong Kong.</p>
<p>Bouygues said in a statement it would carry out the work for Haeco (Hong Kong Aircraft Engineering Co Ltd), a unit of Swire which owns Cathay Pacific which will be the main user of the new equipment.</p>
<p>The contract involves building repair hangars big enough to house five 747 jumbo jets, offices and workshops.</p>
<p>The work will begin this month and be completed in April 1998 before the opening of the new airport.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
